{"schema":"LAW_EN_DOCUMENT_V1","id":"i18n-898b6be348c1826143b0be059701334a3060dac07d5aefa1","family_id":"KR:012159","country":"KR","language":"en","title":"Special Act on Investigating the Truth of the April 16 Sewol Ferry Disaster and Building a Safe Society","title_original":"4ㆍ16세월호참사 진상규명 및 안전사회 건설 등을 위한 특별법","kind":"법률","source_version":"284117","promulgated":null,"effective":null,"translation_status":"AI_DRAFT","body_status":"BODY_LOADED","source_url":"https://www.law.go.kr/LSW/lsInfoP.do?lsiSeq=284117","source_sha256":"c141291f23520264444e31f7c7002ae169ff7b5f49b50f81aade863d8c364da6","body_sha256":"c010936921840f53e69ca6f1aa998a851ceec99e02f25887e4a6a5b2b3ced164","article_count":1,"full_text":"Article 43 (Protection of Activities of Inquest, etc.) (1) No person shall assault or intimidate a Commissioner or employee of the Inquest, a member of an advisory organ, or an appraiser performing his/her duties, or obstruct the performance of such duties by fraudulent means. \n  (2) No person shall be accorded any unfavorable treatment, such as dismissal, suspension, reduction of salary, or transfer to another position, on the ground that he/she has provided information or attempted to provide information in relation to the investigation.\n  (3) The Inquest shall formulate measures for protecting witnesses, appraisers, and reference witnesses, as well as for securing related materials or things and preventing the destruction thereof.  \n  (4) The Inquest may provide necessary support, including the payment of compensation, and proposal of pardon, to a person who presents testimony or statement or submits materials or things important for the investigation. \n  (5) The details of support and procedures for providing support under paragraph (4), and other necessary matters, shall be prescribed by rules of the Inquest.\n","metadata":{"author_method":"Exact held-source units translated or completed using explicitly recorded source/target spans; original official records r